WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.290
I was teased a lot because
I'm overweight.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:12.589
"Wouldn't it be quicker if you just smeared that on your thighs?"
 /laughter/ "Can you say carbs?"

00:00:12.589 --> 00:00:17.200
A lot of it was behind my back but then
a lot of it was also to my face.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.189
"You're a disgusting, fat pig!"

00:00:19.189 --> 00:00:20.939
Which,

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:23.149
made me feel terrible.

00:00:23.149 --> 00:00:27.149
My name is Emme, and as the first plus size
supermodel, Trust me! I know what it's

00:00:27.149 --> 00:00:30.019
like to be judged based on my size.

00:00:30.019 --> 00:00:31.859
But I'm also a mom

00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:34.460
and now one of my life's greatest passions is

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.420
to be part of

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:42.110
creating a world where children can grow
up happy, successful and fulfilled at any size.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:46.290
Obesity in children and adults has
doubled in the past twenty years.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.840
Alarmingly, it's tripled in teens.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:54.290
Children as young as three years old
view overweight peers as mean, stupid,

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:56.340
ugly, unhappy, lazy,

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:00.210
having few friends and undesirable as playmates.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:04.150
"Hey Ralph."

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:10.840
"Hey Ralph! What's that? Your lunch box?" /laughter/
My friend was picked on by a teacher. He called her

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:15.010
chubby and stuff and i just thought i was
very uncalled for and a teacher shouldn't

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.990
say anything like that.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.810
People are afraid of what's different from them.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:23.860
'Oh, look at that shirt she was wearing, her stomach's
popping out and everything.'

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.650
'Wide load coming through.'

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.710
It just felt wrong.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:29.690
I felt like I couldn't do anything about it.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.270
Many students face this torment daily.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.370
It takes a toll

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.880
or on their emotional

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:35.950
and physical health.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:39.760
One study even found that the quality of
life for obese children

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.060
is as low as children with

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.060
cancer.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.520
"Oh, God, here comes the earthquake." /laughter/

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:51.020
Weight bias is a very socially acceptable
in North American society; it's rarely

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.380
challenged and it's often ignored.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:57.440
Victims of weight bias are more
susceptible to loneliness, depression, 

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.540
anxiety,

00:01:58.540 --> 00:01:59.640
low self-esteem,

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:00.990
poor body image,

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:04.710
and suicidal thoughts and behaviors.
We believe that there's a 

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:07.200
strong social injustice occurring here.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.610
The hundreds of millions of people
around the world are deeply affected by

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:11.489
this

00:02:11.489 --> 00:02:14.049
and it just doesn't need to occur.

00:02:14.049 --> 00:02:18.149
Race bias doesn't need to occur and gender bias doesn't
need to occur for and weight bias

00:02:18.149 --> 00:02:20.049
doesn't need to occur.

